0],[1571,4599],[870,4598],[1334,4597],[1118,4597],[1210,4597],[789,4596],[801,4596],[782,4595],[783,4594],[952,4593],[835,4592],[1328,4591],[1204,4590],[1331,4589],[852,4588],[850,4587],[849,4586],[1413,4585],[1422,4584],[1510,4583],[1024,4582],[999,4581],[1067,4580],[984,4579],[1220,4578],[1288,4577],[1555,4576],[1554,4575],[1466,4574],[1437,4573],[1500,4572],[938,4571],[1281,4570],[1398,4569],[1305,4568],[980,4567],[1505,4566],[1031,4565],[1451,4564],[1570,4563],[893,4562],[1575,4561],[975,4560],[1503,4559],[1549,4558],[1565,4557],[1078,4556],[1077,4556],[1068,4555],[1091,4554],[1191,4553],[1568,4552],[1495,4551],[1449,4550],[1535,4549],[1533,4548],[1531,4547],[858,4546],[1576,4545],[1259,4544],[1054,4544],[1185,4543],[1157,4542],[1209,4542],[1179,4541],[1175,4540],[1224,4539],[1139,4538],[1205,4538],[1109,4537],[1312,4536],[1129,4535],[1203,4534],[1116,4533],[826,4532],[866,4531],[778,4530],[1348,4529],[1200,4528],[911,4527],[824,4526],[910,4525],[754,4524],[1298,4523],[771,4522],[1301,4521],[1101,4520],[1111,4519],[1202,4518],[875,4517],[1037,4516],[1017,4515],[1272,4514],[1064,4513],[838,4512],[839,4511],[834,4510],[1186,4509],[1009,4508],[1315,4507],[1198,4506],[887,4505],[1197,4504],[1199,4503],[796,4502],[1289,4501],[1104,4500],[853,4499],[1365,4498],[1286,4497],[1032,4496],[1013,4495],[1268,4494],[1014,4493],[1098,4492],[1285,4491],[845,4490],[1280,4489],[1151,4488],[909,4487],[1270,4486],[786,4485],[868,4484],[966,4483],[901,4482],[1005,4481],[956,4480],[805,4479],[880,4478],[1180,4477],[1174,4476],[1250,4475],[1231,4474],[830,4473],[1135,4472],[1211,4471],[1028,4470],[1090,4469],[1075,4468],[766,4467],[1126,4466],[1402,4465],[1499,4464],[949,4463],[1003,4462],[814,4461],[1016,4460],[810,4459],[1284,4458],[1226,4457],[816,4456],[1346,4455],[1461,4454],[1526,4453],[1412,4452],[1060,4451],[1152,4450],[1447,4449],[862,4448],[1468,4447],[1274,4446],[928,4445],[1276,4444],[856,4443],[1093,4442],[970,4441],[963,4440],[825,4439],[922,4438],[1479,4437],[1455,4436],[1453,4435],[780,4434],[904,4433],[873,4432],[1409,4431],[937,4430],[1044,4429],[747,4428],[1190,4427],[812,4426],[998,4425],[1325,4424],[1008,4423],[1415,4422],[742,4421],[1177,4420],[768,4419],[1269,4418],[1322,4417],[1176,4416],[1195,4415],[932,4414],[761,4413],[1120,4412],[1194,4411],[758,4410],[756,4409],[757,4408],[1169,4407],[1018,4406],[987,4405],[1230,4404],[811,4403],[1022,4402],[929,4401],[1287,4400],[1026,4399],[1105,4398],[1173,4397],"You'll also need to be logged in with the Azure CLI and have the necessary\npermissions to manage the resources in our Azure subscription (more on this\nhere).","You usually don't have to go looking for problems: Prometheus evaluates alert\nrules and Alertmanager sends them to our **Telegram** alert chat. Critical alerts\nrepeat every hour, warnings every 12 hours. Among others, you get alerted when:","You still need the Azure CLI to manage secrets in Key Vault and to inspect Azure\nresources.","You rarely need this: day-to-day changes go through Flux. Run Ansible when you\nchange something under `ansible/` (e.g. a K3s upgrade or a new backup target).\nOnly the IT Lead group has access to the node.","You need the Azure CLI, logged in with an account that has the\n**Key Vault Secrets Officer** role on the vault.","You don't need `az aks get-credentials` or `kubelogin` anymore: those were only\nneeded for the old AKS cluster.","You don't deploy from your machine: you open a PR, and once it's merged into `main`,\nFlux applies it.  \nCheck minikube or K3s to run a k8s cluster on your machine for testing purposes.","You can find more about our benefits here.","You can add (or update) a secret with the following command:","With WARP connected, SSH into the node:","Why We Use Terraform","Why Kubernetes on a single VM instead of plain Docker?\nKubernetes gives us declarative deployments, rolling updates, health checks and\nper-application resource limits. Flux keeps the cluster in sync with Git, so the\n`polinetwork-cd` repository is always the source of truth for what is running.","Why K3s instead of a managed cluster?\nUntil October 2026 we ran on AKS (Azure Kubernetes Service). K3s gives us the\nsame Kubernetes API on one VM that we fully control and size ourselves, and it\ndrops our dependency on AKS-specific add-ons (Azure CSI drivers, Longhorn, ArgoCD).","Why","While the choices made in this implementation reflect our specific requirements\nand constraints, it's worth noting that other approaches exist for managing\ncloud infrastructure with Terraform.","While Terraform is responsible for infrastructure, **PoliNetwork-CD** focuses on **managing the lifecycle of applications** running on that infrastructure, ensuring that code changes are applied automatically and securely.","Where","Whenever there is `<something>` in the code or in a command, that's a parameter you need to set.","What runs *inside* the VM is not managed here: see K3s Node and Flux.","What is Terraform?","What is Flux?","What Ansible sets up","What","Welcome to the documentation for the **polinetworkorg/terraform** repository.\nThis page provides an in-depth look at our Terraform implementation on\n**Microsoft Azure**, detailing the architecture of our infrastructure and the\nkey modules that make it up. While this overview highlights our main components,\nit’s important to note that there are alternative approaches to similar problems,\nand our setup is tailored to our current needs.","Welcome to PoliNetwork's technical documentation! This documentation is intended\nto provide a somewhat comprehensive guide to many of PoliNetwork's projects.","Welcome (con gruppi per semestre e anno)","websites reach the cluster through a **Cloudflare Tunnel** (an outbound connection\nopened by `cloudflared` pods running in the cluster);","Web UI","Web dashboards","We use k8s to deploy our applications, on our K3s node.  \nEach app is a folder of plain k8s manifests in the\npolinetwork-cd repository, tied\ntogether with Kustomize. Helm Charts\nare possible too, through a Flux `HelmRelease` (see `infrastructure/external-secrets` for an example).","We use an **Azure Storage Account** for managing the Terraform state. The state\nfiles are stored within a dedicated container named `terraform-state`,\nas defined in our **storage** module:","We run our infrastructure on Azure (paid with the\nMicrosoft Azure Sponsorship)","We rely on Flux to deploy our pods following the manifests in the `main` branch of polinetwork-cd.\nFlux continuously compares the cluster with the repository and applies any difference, so a merged PR in polinetwork-cd reaches production within minutes.","We have two Key Vaults, one per trust boundary:","Voto e commento professori","Volumes are not backed up automatically. If you add an app with data worth keeping\n(see Add Storage), add it to\n`ansible/roles/backup/templates/k3s-application-backup.sh.j2` in polinetwork-cd, using\nthe right tool for the data:","Volumes are **not** backed up automatically. The application backup on the node\nonly includes the databases and directories it knows about. If the new volume\nholds data we can't afford to lose, add it to the backup script: see\nBackups.","Volume directories stay on disk anyway (`reclaimPolicy: Retain`), under\n`/srv/<fast|standard>/volumes/<k8s-namespace>/`.","Voice Recogniser","Virtual Assistant","variabili locali","Use the secret in a pod","Use the same `<k8s-namespace>` value for the folder name, the `Namespace` resource and\nthe `namespace` field of `kustomization.yaml`. You don't need to write the namespace in\nthe other manifests: Kustomize adds it.","Use the Kubernetes secret in the pod","Use environment variables instead. Mounting the\nSecret as a volume was required by the old CSI driver; with ESO it's only extra\nYAML, and no app does it anymore. Keep it for an app that can only read its\nconfiguration from files.","Uptime Kuma: is each public website up?","uploads it to the private `backups` container of the `polinetworkbackups`\nstorage account, using the `id-k3s-backup` managed identity;","Upgrading K3s","Updating a secret value","Update `k3s_version`, `k3s_release_url` and `k3s_sha256` in `ansible/vars/main.yml`.","Typing","Two systemd timers on the node, installed by Ansible (`ansible/roles/backup`), back up the cluster:","Transition","Traefik picks the app from the `Ingress` whose `host` matches, and forwards the\nrequest to that app's `Service`.","Tools needed","Tol Project (con anche resoconto dei punteggi svolti e grafico dell'andamento dei progressi)","ToDo Backend","Toast","To stop Flux from touching an app while you debug it by hand, **suspend** its\nKustomization from the Web UI. Remember to **resume** it afterwards: a suspended\napp also stops receiving image updates.","To stop an app temporarily, **suspend** its Kustomization in the\nFlux Web UI and scale it down from the node:","To run terraform commands you need to have the right permissions and credentials.\nIf you are not sure about your permissions, please contact the IT department (but\nif you have to ask you probably shouldn't run `apply` yourself anyway).","To run from inside the VM (for example through Azure Run Command), put a reviewed\ncheckout on the VM and run:","To deploy our applications, we use Flux syncing the\n`clusters/k3s` folder of the `main` branch of\npolinetwork-cd.","To check if everything is working, run `k3s kubectl get pods -n <namespace>`. You should see a list of pods.","To bring it back, **resume** the Kustomization: Flux restores the replicas from Git.","To access services running on the cluster (such as the PostgreSQL database), you\nneed two hops: `kubectl port-forward` on the node, and an SSH tunnel from your\nmachine to the node. You can do both with one command:","To **update/re-set** that secret, during the 90 days retention period, you must recover it first,\nthen run the command to update it","Title [prop della page]: tommaso","Tipo di Corso","Through Flux, the repository is used to:","Three layers, three tools:","this will open a shell inside a pod of that deployment (use `/bin/bash` if the image has it). \nMind there is no `screen` installed by default but you can use `nohup`.","This will give you a breakdown of all the pods running in the infrastructure.\nBesides one namespace per app (`web`, `backend`, `postgres`, ...), you'll see:","This tutorial assumes your account has the right permissions to access the infrastructure. If not, please contact the team.\nSSH access to the node is restricted to the **IT Lead** group.","This section provides a basic guide on how to update our infrastructure using\nTerraform and introduces some of the automated workflows that help us maintain\nconsistency and control.","This section explains how we organized our infrastructure.","This is the crucial part, so make sure to follow it step-by-step.","This is one of the core reasons we are structured as a nonprofit organization, and why\nwe use Azure as our cloud provider.","This has to be run as soon as you clone the repository or when you pull changes\nthat include new modules or providers. Locally, add\n`-backend-config=use_oidc=false` (OIDC is only for GitHub Actions).","This documentation assumes you already have the Terraform CLI installed on your\nlocal machine. If you need help setting up Terraform, please refer to the\nofficial documentation.","This clear separation between code, Terraform state, and the actual cloud state\nis key to maintaining a reliable and predictable infrastructure.","These files hold personal data and credentials in clear text. Delete them as soon as\nyou're done.","These are some useful operations on existing apps.","There is no need to set the namespace in the `ExternalSecret`: Kustomize sets it\nfrom the `namespace` field of `kustomization.yaml`.","There is no kubeconfig to download: you SSH into the node and run `kubectl` there.","There are two storage classes, one per data disk:","There are three required steps:","Then run the playbook (see K3s Node):\n`verify.yml` takes a fresh backup and checks it.","Then add it to the list:","The workload identity trust relies on the cluster's service-account signing key,\nwhose public part is committed in Terraform\n(`environments/k3s/k3s-service-account-jwks.json`). If the node is rebuilt from\nscratch without restoring the control-plane backup, the key changes and that file\nmust be updated, otherwise External Secrets can't read Key Vault.","The volume is created when the first pod using it is scheduled, so the PVC stays\n`Pending` until then: that's expected.","The VM never accepts inbound connections from the Internet: the tunnel is an\noutbound connection, and outbound traffic leaves Azure through a NAT Gateway.","The VM has no public IP and the NSG denies all inbound traffic. The host\nfirewall drops everything except SSH, the node itself and cluster traffic.","The storage account only accepts traffic from the K3s subnet, so download backups from the node.","The script is the only supported way to apply changes. It runs the playbook in\ncheck mode, then applies it twice and fails if the second run still changes\nsomething (the playbook must be idempotent). Finally it runs\n`playbooks/verify.yml`, which checks the disks, the K3s version, the firewall,\nthe SSH configuration, that Flux is ready, that pods can't reach Azure IMDS, and\nit takes and validates a fresh backup. Logs are saved in `ansible/artifacts/`\n(ignored by Git).","The rules live in `apps/monitoring/prometheus/alert-rules.yml` in polinetwork-cd.","The rest of the docs write `kubectl` and assume this alias.","The provisioning playbook (`ansible/playbooks/provision.yml`) applies these roles, in order:","The possible values of ```<namespace>``` match the folders in\n`apps/` in the\npolinetwork-cd repository (e.g. `web`, `backend`, `postgres`). Run\n`kubectl get namespaces` to see them all.","The polinetwork-cd repository has its own CI too: the **Ansible** workflow lints the playbooks and builds every Flux path with `kustomize` on each pull request. See K3s Node.","The playbooks run from your machine against `10.43.1.4` over SSH, so connect\nWARP first.","The pieces, all in polinetwork-cd:","The node only has the age **public** key. The private key (the \"identity\") is the\nsecret `backup-age-identity` in the `kv-pn-infra` Key Vault, and it must never be\ncopied to the node. Without it, the backups can't be read.","the node is short on CPU, memory, disk space or inodes;","The node is ARM64. Every image we deploy must have a `linux/arm64` variant,\notherwise the pod fails with `exec format error`. Our GitHub workflows publish\nmulti-arch images (`amd64` + `arm64`) for this reason.","The node is ARM64. An image built only for `amd64` can't run there, and the pod fails\nwith `exec format error`. Build a multi-arch image (see the\nweb workflow\nfor an example), or check that the third-party image you use publishes `linux/arm64`.","the network: `vnet-k3s` (`10.43.0.0/16`), a NAT Gateway for outbound traffic,\nand an NSG that denies all inbound traffic;","the managed identities, including the one External Secrets uses through\nworkload identity federation, and the public OIDC issuer the cluster's\nservice-account tokens are verified against.","The last 7 days are on the node, in `/srv/standard/backups/k3s-applications/`,\nreadable only by root. Copy the one you need to your home:","the Key Vaults `kv-pn-apps` (application secrets) and `kv-pn-infra`\n(platform secrets);","The k3s01 VM, how Ansible configures it, and how to run the playbooks.","The K3s node `k3s01` has **no public IP**. Its private address is `10.43.1.4`,\ninside the Azure VNet `vnet-k3s`, and the Azure firewall (NSG) denies all inbound\ntraffic. Nothing reaches the VM directly from the Internet:","The integrated leasing mechanism provided\nby the Azure Storage Account is used for state locking, ensuring that concurrent\nTerraform operations do not conflict with each other.","The inputs are named after the provider, with hyphens turned into underscores:\nthe provider `bot-ts-image` becomes `inputs.bot_ts_image`.","the image would **not update** if you **don't follow** this guide, even though there is `latest`:\nthe node already has an image called `nginx:latest` and has no reason to pull it again.","The image must be **public** on GHCR: neither Flux nor the node use registry credentials.\nUsing the GHCR package `ghcr.io/polinetworkorg/<image>`:","The full procedure is in Setup.","The Flux Operator is upgraded the same way (`flux_operator_*` and\n`flux_distribution_version`).","The first time, your browser asks you to authenticate. You don't need an SSH key:\nCloudflare issues a short-lived certificate for the `pnadmin` user, and the node\nonly accepts keys and Cloudflare Access certificates (no passwords, no root login).","The first step of our CI processes is the GitHub Actions workflow in each repository. For example, the web repository has:","The control-plane backup is only needed to rebuild the node from scratch: it restores\nthe K3s datastore, including the service-account signing key that Azure workload\nidentity trusts.","The code is split into two independent **root modules** (the folders you run\n`terraform` in). Each root owns its resources and has its own state file; a root\ncan only read the other's resources through data sources, never declare them.","The code in **Terraform** describes these resources declaratively: it defines the desired state, and Terraform applies the necessary changes to reach that state. This repository is primarily used to **create and modify the cloud infrastructure** where applications will run.","the Cloudflare tunnel has no connections (all public websites are down);","The bundled **Traefik** stays as the ingress controller, but Flux turns its\nService into `ClusterIP`: only `cloudflared` reaches it.","The best place to start is going through the Getting Started section to get a high level overview of how things are organized.  \nIf you're looking for a guide on how to achieve a specific outcome, you can look in the Guides.","The API server signs service-account tokens for a public OIDC issuer\n(`pnk3soidc` storage account). Azure trusts that issuer, which is how External\nSecrets reads Key Vault without any stored credential.","The AKS cluster `aks-polinetwork` is still defined in the `environments/legacy`\nTerraform root, but no production workload runs on it anymore.\nIf you find instructions mentioning `az aks get-credentials`, ArgoCD,\n`SecretProviderClass` or Longhorn (e.g. in old READMEs), they refer to the AKS setup.","The `Recreate` strategy avoids two pods writing to the same volume during a rollout.","The `prune: disabled` annotation keeps Flux from deleting the namespace, and with it\neverything inside, if the app is removed from Git by mistake.","The `kustomize.toolkit.fluxcd.io/prune: disabled` annotation keeps Flux from deleting the\nPVC if it disappears from Git (e.g. a bad refactor). CI rejects PVCs without it.","the `k3s01` VM (Debian 13 ARM64) and its two data disks, `disk-k3s-fast`\n(Premium SSD v2, 64 GB) and `disk-k3s-standard` (Standard SSD, 128 GB);","The `flux` CLI isn't installed on the node, but the Flux resources are regular\nKubernetes objects:","The `config.json` files with `\"disabled\": true` you may find at the root of polinetwork-cd\nbelong to the old ArgoCD setup. Flux doesn't read them.","The `BackupStale` alert fires on Telegram when there has been no successful\napplication backup for 7 hours or no control-plane backup for 26 hours.\n`BackupMetricsMissing` fires if the metrics disappear altogether.","The `<k8s-namespace>` should be a slug (lowercase words separated by hyphens) identifier of the application/service you want to deploy.","The **Terraform** repository is responsible for managing and provisioning cloud infrastructure. In simple terms, it defines and creates the resources needed for the infrastructure, such as:","The **polinetworkorg/terraform** repository is our centralized solution for\nprovisioning and managing cloud infrastructure on Azure. Its default branch is\n**`stable`**.","The **PoliNetwork-CD** (Continuous Deployment) repository picks up where Terraform stops. It has two parts:","The **Ansible** workflow in polinetwork-cd runs on every pull request that\ntouches `ansible/`, `clusters/k3s/`, `infrastructure/`, `apps/` or `tests/`. It\nruns `ansible-lint`, `shellcheck`, a playbook syntax check, `kustomize build` on\nevery Flux path and the manifest tests in `tests/`. It does **not** touch the VM.","Terraform stops at the Azure boundary: it creates the VM, but it doesn't configure\nwhat runs inside it.","Terraform Repository","Terraform operates through a simple yet powerful workflow:","Terraform is an open-source Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tool developed by\nHashiCorp. It allows you to define, provision, and manage the infrastructure\nusing a declarative configuration language. This means you describe the desired\nstate of the infrastructure, and Terraform takes care of creating and updating\nthe resources to match that state.","Terraform Implementation Overview","Terraform Documentation","Terraform Code vs. Terraform State vs. Azure State","Terraform","TASTO AGGIORNA","takes consistent online copies (no app is stopped);","TabelleCalendar","TabelleArticle","TabellaGroups","Swipe for PoliTinder - PoliMeet","Suddivisione compiti:\nFrontend & logica: Elia P. – Tommaso M. – Luke P. – Giacomo M. – Federico G. (Jolly)\nAPI & Backend: Diego A. – Federico A. – Paolo R.\nDesign: tutto il resto\nPR: Giulia","stessa cosa per quanto riguarda reazioni a articoli, materiali da scaricare per orientare meglio l’utente\nanche in base a chi già ha letto/scaricato quel tipo di documento.","State Management","SSH into the node, then run","SSH into the node with ```ssh pnadmin@10.43.1.4```","SSH","spigoli raccordati","slider per aggiornamenti (?) forse","Slider orizzontale [container]: tommaso","Skip this and the `ExternalSecret` stays `NotReady` with an error saying the\nstore doesn't allow the namespace.","sincronizzazione","Since a volume is just a directory, you can look at it from the node:","Si pensava a usarle come reazioni ad esempio agli eventi creati dall’utente e/o quelli previsti\ndal calendario accademico\nes. l’utente mette la reazione e il giorno dell’evento gli arriverà la notifica con titolo ed emoji\nabbinata (da capire come mettere in grafica)","Shop per feature","Setup","Selettore di lingua – Tray: giacomo","See this section.","See Add Storage for how volumes are carved out of these disks.","Sede","Security guardrails","Secrets are used to configure deployments with **sensitive** data like database login, API keys, and so on.  \nSecrets live in **Azure Key Vault** and never in Git. The\nExternal Secrets Operator (ESO), running in the\ncluster, copies them into regular Kubernetes `Secret`s that your pods can use.","Search bar: giacomo","Search Bar","Se non siete familiare con typescript potreste trovarvi in difficoltà con il definire un paio di\ntipi e essere tentati ad usare `any`.","SCHERMATE:","schermate","Running the playbooks","Running Terraform commands can modify the cloud infrastructure.","Run the following command","Run kubectl as ```k3s kubectl``` (or add the alias ```alias kubectl='k3s kubectl'```)","Run `kubectl get svc -n <namespace>` on the node to find service names and ports.\nYou can use the same template to connect to other services.","Run ```az login``` to login.","roles","Risultato:","Ricerca Aule Libere con Navigatore (gps)","Retention","Restoring overwrites live data. Agree on it with the Direttivo first, and take a\nfresh backup right before (`sudo systemctl start k3s-application-backup.service`)\nso you can go back.","Restoring","ResourceSets","Repository Overview","Repository layout","Replace `clusters/k3s/apps/<k8s-namespace>.yaml` with a `ResourceSet` that renders the\nsame Kustomization, plus an `images` override with the digest:","Remove it from every `ExternalSecret` first, otherwise the `ExternalSecret` turns\n`NotReady`. Then delete it with:","Remove an app","Remove `<k8s-namespace>.yaml` from `clusters/k3s/apps/kustomization.yaml` and delete the\nfile and the `apps/<k8s-namespace>/` folder. Remove its provider and receiver entry too,\nif it had automatic image updates.","Register the app with Flux","References","Redis: the `redis_snapshot` helper.","QUESTIONE EMOJI","Questa cosa va assolutamente evitata ad ogni costo perché è l'unico modo per far spuntare fuori bug\nantipatici dove non si riesce a capire perché le cose non funzionano.","publishes its success time to Prometheus.","Publish it on a domain","Publish a Docker image with an **`arm64`** variant","Public traffic arrives through the Cloudflare Tunnel to Traefik, which routes it by\nhostname. Two things are needed.","prop dei componenti","Production runs on a single VM, **`k3s01`**, created by Terraform\n(`environments/k3s`) and configured by the Ansible playbooks in\n`polinetwork-cd/ansible`.","Production runs on **K3s**, a lightweight Kubernetes distribution, installed on\na single Azure ARM64 VM called `k3s01`. Around it there are a few Azure services\n(Key Vault, Managed Disks, Blob Storage, Entra ID) and Cloudflare, which\npublishes our websites through a tunnel and gives us SSH access to the VM.","Procedure","Prima installazione su server","Prefix the Key Vault secret name with the app that owns it, e.g. `backend-encryption-key`.\nKey Vault names allow only letters, digits and hyphens.","Pre-Commits","Port Forwarding","polinetworkorg/terraform - Contains the Terraform code for the Azure resources: the `k3s01` VM, its disks and network, the Key Vaults, the managed identities, the backup storage account.","polinetworkorg/polinetwork-cd - Our GitOps repo. It contains the Ansible playbooks that turn the VM into a K3s node, and the Kubernetes manifests of every app and service. Flux, running in the cluster, applies them.","PoliNetwork's Technical Documentation","PoliNetwork-CD Repository","PoliMeet (PoliTinder)","PoliFemo","poliassoc","Poi fare un commit senza uscire dalla sessione SSH, se si riavvia correttamente si può uscire.","Pods cannot reach the Azure Instance Metadata Service (`169.254.169.254`), so\nthey can't borrow the VM's managed identities.","Plus `my-app` in the `kv-pn-apps` store conditions, as shown above.","Please don't report issues or PRs on this section, we are already busy as it is 🙃","Platform components (`infrastructure/`)","Pick a release from K3s releases and\ndownload its `k3s-arm64` binary checksum.","Piattaforma","per visualizzare i colori nella cartella design\\palette e' consigliato scaricare _Color Highlight_","per tanto qua sotto porrò un paio di semplici esempi di cose non completamente intuitive per evitare\ndi ritrovarvi senza definizione di tipi","Per opzione sincronizza:\ncosa sincronizzare?\ngoogle, altro? sistema?","Per la documentazione tecnica si può usare Markdown in combinazione con mermaid.js","people reach the VM through **Cloudflare WARP**, which routes `10.43.1.4` through\nthe same tunnel, and **Cloudflare Access for Infrastructure**, which signs a\nshort-lived SSH certificate after you log in with your PoliNetwork account.","Paste the secret value into a text file (no extension or \".txt\" is valid) on a **single line**","Parametri:","Parameters:","Page: tommaso","packs them in a `.tar.gz` with a `SHA256SUMS` file and encrypts it with\nage;","Overview","Ours is installed by Ansible through the\nFlux Operator, and it syncs the\n**`main`** branch of\npolinetwork-cd, starting\nfrom the `clusters/k3s` folder.","Our repository is organized to clearly separate concerns and promote reusability.\nWhile the exact folder structure may vary, a typical layout looks like this:","Our organization leverages Terraform to manage our Azure cloud infrastructure for several important reasons:","Our modular design, state management strategy,\nand access controls are tailored to our current operational needs and funding\nsituation—but they are not set in stone. Please feel free to reach out to the\nIT department if you have any questions or suggestions.","Our K3s node is ARM64, so the `arm64` build is required. Keep publishing a\nmulti-arch `latest` manifest when you set up a new repository.","Our infrastructure is deployed on Azure West Europe (Amsterdam).\nThe Azure resources are described in Terraform (IaC) in the\nterraform repository.","Our deployments use rolling updates with `maxUnavailable: 0`: Kubernetes starts the new pod, waits for its readiness probe, and only then stops the old one, so a broken image doesn't take the app down.\nStateful services (databases, Redis, Grafana) use the `Recreate` strategy instead, because only one pod at a time can write to their volume.","Otherwise create it:","orario lezione","Options","Optionally, publish it on a domain, add secrets, add storage and enable automatic image updates","Open a PR, merge it, then run `./scripts/provision-and-verify.sh`. K3s restarts\nwith the new binary; workloads come back on their own.","Open a PR into polinetwork-cd. Once it's merged, Flux applies it. Then, from the node:","Open a PR into polinetwork-cd, wait for CI, merge","Once you verified you have sufficient space available, add the PVC to the app manifest:","Once you have logged in to the Azure CLI, select the subscription and export it\nfor the provider:","Once merged, Flux deletes the app's resources, except the ones annotated with\n`prune: disabled`: the namespace, the PVCs and, for apps with automatic image\nupdates, the generated Kustomization. Delete those by hand from the node once you're\nsure the data is not needed:","ogni file deve essere leggibile dentro a VScode quindi bisogna usare md per tutti i documenti di testo\nse si utilizzano estensioni particolari che risulatno essenzali bisogna inserirle dentro a questo README nella sezione apposita.","Notifiche da PoliAssocizioni, Polimi, etc...","Note that no modifications or updates will probably be made to these documents,\nand they might be removed in the future.","Notable K3s settings","Normally you shouldn't SSH into a pod to execute repetitive commands, instead you should configure them in the Dockerfile of your application.\nTo connect into a pod's terminal, first SSH into the node, then use the `kubectl exec` command like so","None of these documents are actively maintained. The information provided may be\noutdated or inaccurate.","nomi di tipi e interfacce di typescript","Nome gruppo (obbligatorio)","news","New images don't need a commit: when a new `latest` image is published, GitHub calls a Flux webhook, Flux resolves `latest` to the new image digest and rolls out the deployment.\nIf the webhook is missed, Flux checks for new images every 6 hours anyway.","Never copy a private SSH key or a secret value into the repository or into Azure\nRun Command parameters.","Navigation","Naming","Most of the docs explain procedures with `kubectl`, which you run on the K3s node\nover SSH, and with the Azure CLI, which you use for Key Vault secrets.\nMake sure to set up your access to follow along.","Most of our apps are deployed from the `latest` tag of an image on\nGHCR. A tag can point to a\ndifferent image over time, so Flux resolves it to a **digest** and deploys that\ndigest. When the digest changes, the app rolls out the new image.","More about this in the repository README.","Monitoring","Monitor the deploy on the Flux Web UI","Microsoft Azure Documentation","metodi, attributi e proprietà","Mermaid Class Diagrams","Merging to `main` in polinetwork-cd **is** deploying to production.\nNever `kubectl apply` or `kubectl edit` a resource that Flux manages: Flux reverts\nit at the next reconciliation.","Menu","membri di oggetti e parametri delle funzioni","Materiali Scaricabili da Gitlab e WeBeep","materiali","Maps","Many applications and services need a physical volume or storage to store their data or configuration.  \nOn K3s, volumes are plain directories on the node's data disks, created on demand by the\nlocal-path provisioner when a\nPVC asks for one.\nWe replaced Longhorn and the Azure Managed Disk volumes we used on AKS with it.","Making Changes to the Infrastructure","Look at the `READY`, `STATUS` and `RESTARTS` columns: a pod that is not `Running`,\nor whose restart count keeps growing, needs a look. Some useful follow-ups:","Login in Azure CLI using az login","login (non obbligatorio)","local-path directories are owned by `root`. If your container runs as a non-root\nuser, set `securityContext.fsGroup` on the pod to the user's group (see `apps/redis`\nfor an example).","Lista delle API che servono","Link a Gruppi (con consigliati in base ai propri interessi)","Lingua","lightmode","Let's discover **PoliNetwork's Infrastructure in less than 5 minutes**.","Let the GitHub webhook trigger it:","Le emoji, se usate, sono consentite solo quelle di Unicode 11 in giù (11,10,9, ecc...) per questioni di retrocompatibilità.\nSito ufficiale delle emoji di Unicode https://emojipedia.org/unicode-11.0/","Kubernetes Documentation","Key Vault management","Keep the command running while you use the connection, and stop it with `Ctrl+C`.","Keep in mind that the aim of this guide is not to provide a complete overview of all the commands in the k8s ecosystem but merely to give an easy to read handbook on very basic stuff","K3s Node","K3s Documentation","Introduction","Intro","Installed Icon Pack","Install the Cloudflare WARP client.","Inspecting a volume","inserisci.py","Inserire password a scelta","Infrastructure Structure","Infrastructure","Infracost Documentation","In this section, you will find documentations for archived projects and repositories.\nThese projects are no longer actively maintained or have been deprecated. However,\nthe documentation is preserved for reference purposes and can be valuable for\nunderstanding past developments and decisions. Have at it!","In this section, you will find documentations for archived projects and repositories.\nThese projects are no longer actively maintained or have been deprecated. However,\nthe documentation is preserved for reference purposes and can be valuable for\nunderstanding past developments and decisions.","In summary, **Terraform builds the foundation on which applications run**, while **PoliNetwork-CD sets up the node and manages the deployment and continuous updating of applications**. Both repositories work together to ensure a scalable and efficient cloud infrastructure.","In questo file vengono descritte un paio di indicazioni generali da seguire nelle contribuzioni di\ncodice e qualche guida rapida al fine di aiutare a capire un po' di quirk qua e là","In generale si usa il `camelCase` per cose tipo","In `deployment.yaml`, keep `image: ghcr.io/polinetworkorg/<image>:latest`: the `name`\nunder `images` must match it exactly, and Flux replaces it with the pinned digest.\nSee `clusters/k3s/apps/web.yaml` for a complete example.","impostazioni","Il bottone back in basso a sx: luke","If you want to run Infracost locally, you can install it by following the\nofficial documentation.","If you want to monitor or make changes to the pods:","If you want to manage secrets:","If you want to make changes to the infrastructure:","If you want to learn how it works and how to add new services, check out the\nInfrastructure section.","If you want automatic image updates, write a `ResourceSet` instead of this\n`Kustomization`: see below.","If you try to `set` a secret that has been deleted within the last 90 days without restoring it first, you get the following error:","If you haven't yet set up the Azure CLI please refer to the setup guide.","If you have access to the adminorg account, you can check the current status of\nour Azure grant here.","If you ever happen to be as much as tempted of using `terraform destroy`, you\nbetter be **SURE AS SHIT** about what you are doing. Never run it without\n`-chdir`, and remember the K3s data disks have `prevent_destroy` for a reason. Make sure to review the\nimplications thoroughly before proceeding.","If the secret value is too long or you don't want to copy/paste in terminal (and\nleave it in your shell history) you can use a file instead.","If the app needs another app to be up first (e.g. a database), add it to\n`dependsOn` (e.g. `- name: postgres`).","If it's your first time accessing the infrastructure, you'll need to set up the tools and configure them.","If Cloudflare is down or the tunnel is broken, you can still reach the VM through\n**Azure Run Command** or the **Serial Console** in the Azure portal (VM `k3s01`,\nresource group `rg-polinetwork`). Use them only for emergencies.","icone semplici flat (solo outline?)","https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=naumovs.color-highlight","https://github.com/tabrezansari/React-Native-Virtual-Assistant","https://github.com/react-native-voice/voice#readme","https://github.com/react-native-maps/react-native-maps","https://github.com/raghiii/react-native-vertical-distribution","https://github.com/prscX/react-native-iconic","https://github.com/orjiAce/rn-slick-bottom-tabs?ref=reactnativeexample.com","https://github.com/oblador/react-native-vector-icons","https://github.com/mikalyh/react-navigation-tabbar-collection?ref=reactnativeexample.com","https://github.com/meteor-factory/react-native-tinder-swipe-cards","https://github.com/margelo/react-native-graph?ref=reactnativeexample.com","https://github.com/lottie-react-native/lottie-react-native","https://github.com/localz/react-native-searchbar","https://github.com/junhoyeo/react-native-bubble-tabbar","https://github.com/jeanverster/react-native-styled-toast","https://github.com/jacse/react-native-app-intro-slider","https://github.com/geremih/react-native-circular-action-menu","https://github.com/catalinmiron/react-native-nav-transition","How Terraform Works","How Flux deploys the polinetwork-cd repository to the K3s cluster.","How access works","How a request reaches an app","home","Grid per le cards: luke","Graph","Grafana: node and container metrics from Prometheus.","Given the critical nature of our infrastructure, modifications (e.g., running\n`terraform apply`) are restricted to personnel with sufficient clearance. As an\nassociation, any infrastructure changes require approval from either the Head of\nthe IT Department or the Directive Council. All authorization is managed through\n**Microsoft's Entra ID system**, ensuring that only properly authenticated and\nauthorized users can perform these operations.","Getting Started","funzioni","Funding and Nonprofit Considerations","From the node:","From the node","From the command line","For the other services, stop the app (`kubectl scale --replicas=0`), put the files back\nin its volume under `/srv/<fast|standard>/volumes/<namespace>/<pvc>/`, and scale it up\nagain. Follow the upstream docs for\nRedis and\nInfluxDB.","For PostgreSQL, the dump recreates every database (`--clean --if-exists`), so you can\nstream it into the running server:","For older backups, list and download them from Blob Storage on the node, with the\nbackup identity (its client ID is `backup_identity_client_id` in `ansible/vars/main.yml`):","For more info, check out Flux.","For example, to reach PostgreSQL on `localhost:5432`:","Folders at the root of the repository (`bot-prod/`, `bot-rooms/`, `mariadb/`, ...)\nare leftovers from the AKS era, all disabled. Flux ignores them.","flux.polinetwork.org shows every Kustomization,\nHelmRelease and ResourceSet, with its status, last applied revision and errors.\nYou log in through auth.polinetwork.org; only\nthe Direttivo is admitted. From the UI you can **reconcile** (sync now),\n**suspend** and **resume** any resource.","Flux Web UI: is every app in sync with Git? Why not?","Flux Operator Documentation","Flux only deploys the apps listed in `clusters/k3s/apps/`. Create a Flux\n`Kustomization` for the app:","Flux is a GitOps tool: it runs inside the cluster, watches a\nGit repository and applies whatever it finds there, over and over. If someone\nchanges a resource by hand, Flux puts it back the way Git says. It replaced the\nArgoCD instance we had on AKS.","Flux Documentation","Flux can redeploy the app every time a new `latest` image is published, pinning the\nimage digest (see how it works).  \nThis is an optional feature: the alternative is a fixed version or digest in\n`deployment.yaml` (e.g. `nginx:1.27.4`), bumped with a PR.","Flux","First of all, SSH into the node and check\nhow much space is available on the disk you want to use:","Find an overview of Flux in Flux.","Filtro su titolo","Filtro su categorie","Filtro su autori","Feed Notizie","Features menu: luke","Features da approvare","Features Backend","Features App (in ordine di priorita')","fase personalizzazione iniziale + benvenuto","Example","Everything regarding the deployment of apps and services is divided into two repositories:","ESO reads Key Vault through workload identity federation: no Azure password or\nkey is stored in the cluster.","ESO re-reads Key Vault every `refreshInterval` (1 hour). To pick up a new value\nimmediately, force a sync:","Esempio:","Esempi","Environment variables are read only when a container starts, so restart the app:","Enroll it in PoliNetwork's Cloudflare Zero Trust organization\n(*Preferences → Account → Login to Cloudflare Zero Trust*) and log in with your\nPoliNetwork account. Ask the team for the organization (team) name.","emoji","effetto “vetro” e material (giocoso e dinamico)","ed se caso si può usare anche il `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` per eventuali costanti.","Each run:","Each file here is a Flux\n`Kustomization`\nthat points to one folder of `infrastructure/` or `apps/`. It also sets:","Each app repository builds its Docker image and publishes it to GHCR with the `latest` tag (see CI).\nThat's where the app pipeline stops: it doesn't touch the polinetwork-cd repository.","e il `PascalCase` per le","Download and install the Azure CLI.","download","Don't edit files of a running database from the node. Stop the app first, or go\nthrough the app itself.","Don't add app namespaces to `kv-pn-infra`. It holds the secrets that run the\nplatform itself.","Divisione accademico-personale per tenere ordine\npossibilità di scaricare la schermata ?","Disks","Disable an app","diagrams","Developer","Detailed overview of our Azure-based infrastructure managed via the polinetworkorg/terraform repository.","Design","Deploy and check","Deploy a New App","Delete the file","Delete a secret","Definizioni di funzioni","Definizioni di componenti","Declare the `ExternalSecret`","Declare an `ExternalSecret` in the app folder","Day-to-day","Data inizio pubblicazione notizie","Data fine pubblicazione notizie (opzionale, se non lo si mette vuol dire fino ad ora)","Data e ora inizio","Data e ora fine","Dashboards","darkmode","Create this minimal file structure:","Create the app folder","Create a new branch (named as you like, e.g. `mc-server-deploy`)","Cose che procrastiniamo:","Core Concepts","Copy the encrypted archive to your machine and decrypt it there with\nage and the identity from Key Vault:","Convenzioni","Continuous Integration","Continuous Deployment","Continuous Delivery","Consiglio di fare riferimento al TypeSript Handbook","Consider the following manifest:","Connect WARP to PoliNetwork's Cloudflare Zero Trust organization","Configure the tools","Components","Componenti da dividerci:","componenti (anche se di fatto sono solo funzioni)","Come inserire diagrammi Mermaid nel GitHub-flavored Markdown","Collection of documentations for archived projects and repositories.","Cloudflare WARP and an SSH client (`kubectl` runs on the node)","Cloudflare WARP & SSH","Cloudflare terminates HTTPS, so the `Ingress` only needs the plain `web` entrypoint:\nno certificates in the cluster.","Cloudflare sends the request through the `k3s01` tunnel to one of the two\n`cloudflared` pods in the cluster.","Cloud Infrastructure","Clone polinetwork-cd repo","classi","CI","Check if the app folder already contains an `external-secret.yaml`. If it does,\njust add a new entry.","Chat Bot (Polifemo) (server)","CD","Card: luke","Caratteristiche generali:","caratteristiche","Calendario: elia","Calendario (orari lezioni ed aule)","calendario","By following these steps and leveraging our automated workflows, you ensure that\ninfrastructure changes are managed in a consistent, cost-aware, and controlled\nmanner.","By convention, our apps call both the `ExternalSecret` and the resulting Secret\n`azure-kv`, a name inherited from the AKS setup.","Both vaults have **purge protection** enabled: a deleted secret can't be purged\nbefore its 90 days are over, and its name can't be reused in the meantime unless\nyou recover it.","Basics","Basic Workflow for Infrastructure Changes","Basic Terraform CLI Commands","Backups","Back it up","Azure CLI","Automatic image updates","aule libere","As an environment variable","As a nonprofit organization, we benefit from a **Microsoft Azure Grant for Nonprofits**,\nwhich provides us with a budget of **€2000 per year**. This support helps offset\nour cloud costs and underpins our commitment to maintaining a robust and scalable\ninfrastructure.","As a file (deprecated)","articolo ---> possibilità di download, like/dislike (?)","articles","Archived Projects 🗃️","Apps that don't need automatic updates (databases, monitoring, ...) pin their\nimage in the manifest, and you bump them with a PR.","Apps talk to each other through their Service:\n`http://<service>.<namespace>.svc.cluster.local:<port>`.","Append an entry under `data`:","Api che ritorna le notizie","Api che ritorna le aule libere","Api che ritorna i gruppi","Anything you change inside a pod is lost when the pod restarts, and Flux reverts changes made with `kubectl edit`. Make persistent changes in the polinetwork-cd repository.","Ansible, only for changes to the node itself","Ansible finds the data disks by Azure LUN, refuses to touch a disk that is\nsmaller than expected or holds an unexpected filesystem, formats them only when\nblank and mounts them by UUID. Both disks have `prevent_destroy` in Terraform.","Anno scolastico","Animation","Animated Icons","and add it to the app's `kustomization.yaml`:","an SQLite file: the `sqlite_backup` helper, which takes a consistent copy and archives\nthe other files in the volume;","An admission policy rejects pods using `hostNetwork`, `hostPID` or `hostIPC`\noutside `kube-system`, and another one forbids pods from running as the\n`keyvault-reader` service account.","An `Ingress` in the app folder (and in `kustomization.yaml`):","Always review the execution plan (`terraform plan`) before applying changes.","Always pick a root with `-chdir`, e.g. `terraform -chdir=environments/k3s plan`.\nRunning Terraform at the repository root does nothing useful.","Altre definizioni con Unknown","Allow the namespace to use the store","All the YAML lives in the app folder `apps/<namespace>/` of\npolinetwork-cd.","Alerts","aggiornamento semestrale ---> quanto evidente? notifica nei messaggi? notizia in evidenza?","After the deletion, the secret remains in a `Recoverable State` for **90 days**.  \nDuring this period the secret can be recovered with the following command:","After that, Flux takes over everything inside the cluster (see Flux).","Adding a new app","Add the secret into the Key Vault","Add Storage","Add or update a secret","Add a volume","Add a provider that tracks its `latest` tag:","Add a New Secret","Add a key to an existing `ExternalSecret`","Access and Authorization","About this documentation","A visitor opens e.g. `https://api.polinetwork.org`. DNS points to Cloudflare.","A public hostname on the **`k3s01`** tunnel in the Cloudflare Zero Trust dashboard\n(*Networks → Tunnels*), pointing to Traefik like the existing hostnames. The tunnel\nis managed from the dashboard, not from Git, so ask someone in the Direttivo to add it.","a pod is crash-looping, OOM-killed or not running, or a deployment is missing replicas;","a Flux resource, an `ExternalSecret` or a secret store is not ready;","A few rules we follow for every app:","a database: its own dump/backup command, through `kubectl exec` (like PostgreSQL and InfluxDB);","A complete app that reads one secret, `my-app-api-key`, from `kv-pn-apps`:","a backup hasn't succeeded on schedule.","A `ClusterSecretStore` only serves the namespaces listed in its `conditions`.\nIf your app is new, add its namespace to the `kv-pn-apps` store:","3. Restore the data","2. Decrypt it on your machine","1. Get the archive","| Where | Path                                                                                  | Kept for |\n| ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- |\n| Node  | `/srv/standard/backups/k3s-applications/`, `/srv/standard/backups/k3s-control-plane/` | 7 days   |","| Where        | Path                                                                  | Kept for                            |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| Blob Storage | `backups/k3s-applications/k3s01/`, `backups/k3s-control-plane/k3s01/` | 90 days, immutable for the first 30 |","| URL                  | What                                                            | Who can log in                      |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| flux.polinetwork.org | Flux Web UI: sync status of every app, reconcile/suspend/resume | Direttivo, via auth.polinetwork.org |","| URL                    | What                    | Who can log in |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------------- | -------------- |\n| status.polinetwork.org | Uptime Kuma status page | Public         |","| URL                        | What                                    | Who can log in   |\n| -------------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ---------------- |\n| monitoring.polinetwork.org | Grafana dashboards (Prometheus metrics) | Grafana accounts |","| Storage class | Disk                  | Path on the node                       | Use it for                                                              |\n| ------------- | --------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fast`        | Premium SSD v2, 64 GB | `/srv/fast/volumes/<namespace>/<pvc>/` | Latency-sensitive databases (today: PostgreSQL and the Redis instances) |","| Storage class        | Disk                 | Path on the node                           | Use it for                                                          |\n| -------------------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `standard` (default) | Standard SSD, 128 GB | `/srv/standard/volumes/<namespace>/<pvc>/` | Everything else (today: InfluxDB, Prometheus, Grafana, Uptime Kuma) |","| Root               | State file    |\n| ------------------ | ------------- |\n| `environments/k3s` | `k3s.tfstate` |","| Root                  | State file      |\n| --------------------- | --------------- |\n| `environments/legacy` | `state.tfstate` |","| Role  | What it does                                                                                                |\n| ----- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `k3s` | Installs the pinned K3s binary (checked by SHA-256) and its configuration, waits for the node to be `Ready` |","| Role   | What it does                                                                                              |\n| ------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `flux` | Installs the pinned Flux Operator and the `FluxInstance` that syncs `clusters/k3s` from the `main` branch |","| Role   | What it does                                                                                                     |\n| ------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `base` | Base packages, UTC timezone, `pnadmin` user and the `k3s-admin` group, kernel modules and sysctls for Kubernetes |","| Role     | What it does                                                                 |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `backup` | Installs the encrypted backup scripts and their systemd timers (see Backups) |","| Role      | What it does                                                |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `storage` | Formats and mounts the data disks, creates `/srv/*/volumes` |","| Role       | What it does                                                                                                                                                    |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `security` | SSH hardening (keys and Cloudflare Access certificates only), Debian security updates via `unattended-upgrades` (no automatic reboot), `nftables` host firewall |","| Repository    | Main Purpose                             | Example of Managed Resources               |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| **Terraform** | Creates and manages cloud infrastructure | VM, disks, network, Key Vaults, identities |","| Repository                | Main Purpose                                 | Example of Managed Resources             |\n| ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| **PoliNetwork-CD** (Flux) | Automates application deployment and updates | Deployments, ingresses, secrets, storage |","| Repository                      | Main Purpose      | Example of Managed Resources             |\n| ------------------------------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| **PoliNetwork-CD** (`ansible/`) | Configures the VM | Disk mounts, firewall, SSH, K3s, backups |","| Namespace     | What runs there                   |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `flux-system` | Flux controllers, the Flux Web UI |","| Namespace     | What runs there                      |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `cloudflared` | The two Cloudflare Tunnel connectors |","| Namespace     | What runs there                                                 |\n| ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `kube-system` | K3s components: CoreDNS, Traefik, metrics-server, node-exporter |","| Namespace          | What runs there           |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------- |\n| `external-secrets` | External Secrets Operator |","| Namespace            | What runs there        |\n| -------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| `local-path-storage` | The volume provisioner |","| Mount | Azure disk      | Type                | Used for         |\n| ----- | --------------- | ------------------- | ---------------- |\n| `/`   | `disk-k3s01-os` | Standard SSD, 64 GB | Operating system |","| Mount       | Azure disk              | Type                  | Used for                                        |\n| ----------- | ----------------------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `/srv/fast` | `disk-k3s-fast` (LUN 0) | Premium SSD v2, 64 GB | Volumes of the `fast` storage class (databases) |","| Mount           | Azure disk                  | Type                 | Used for                                                                                      |\n| --------------- | --------------------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `/srv/standard` | `disk-k3s-standard` (LUN 1) | Standard SSD, 128 GB | K3s data (`/srv/standard/k3s`), volumes of the `standard` storage class, local backup staging |","| Layer                                | Tool          | Repository     |\n| ------------------------------------ | ------------- | -------------- |\n| Everything running inside Kubernetes | Flux (GitOps) | polinetwork-cd |","| Layer                                         | Tool    | Repository             |\n| --------------------------------------------- | ------- | ---------------------- |\n| The VM itself (disks, firewall, K3s, backups) | Ansible | polinetwork-cd/ansible |","| Layer                                                        | Tool      | Repository |\n| ------------------------------------------------------------ | --------- | ---------- |\n| Azure resources (VM, disks, network, Key Vaults, identities) | Terraform | terraform  |","| Key Vault    | `ClusterSecretStore` | Contains                                                         | Namespaces allowed to read it          |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `kv-pn-apps` | `kv-pn-apps`         | Application secrets (DB passwords, API keys, OAuth clients, ...) | The app namespaces listed in the store |","| Key Vault     | `ClusterSecretStore` | Contains                                                             | Namespaces allowed to read it |\n| ------------- | -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `kv-pn-infra` | `kv-pn-infra`        | Platform secrets (tunnel token, Flux webhook token, backup key, ...) | `cloudflared`, `flux-system`  |","| Component | What it does                                    |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `traefik` | Makes the bundled Traefik a `ClusterIP` service |","| Component | What it does                                                       |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `storage` | local-path provisioner and the `fast` / `standard` storage classes |","| Component  | What it does                            |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `flux-web` | The Flux Web UI at flux.polinetwork.org |","| Component  | What it does                                                          |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `security` | Admission policies (no host namespaces, no pods as `keyvault-reader`) |","| Component     | What it does                                 |\n| ------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `cloudflared` | The Cloudflare Tunnel connector (2 replicas) |","| Component       | What it does                |\n| --------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `node-exporter` | Node metrics for Prometheus |","| Component       | What it does                                             |\n| --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `secret-stores` | The `kv-pn-apps` and `kv-pn-infra` `ClusterSecretStore`s |","| Component          | What it does                                   |\n| ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `external-secrets` | External Secrets Operator, installed with Helm |","| Component          | What it does                                    |\n| ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `image-automation` | Detects new `latest` images on GHCR (see below) |","| Backup                                      | When (UTC)                                 | Contents                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Applications** (`k3s-application-backup`) | Every 6 hours (00:45, 06:45, 12:45, 18:45) | PostgreSQL (`pg_dumpall`, all databases and roles), Redis (`redis` and `bot-ts` RDB snapshots), InfluxDB (`influx backup`), Uptime Kuma and Grafana (SQLite databases and files) |","| Backup                                         | When (UTC)     | Contents                                                               |\n| ---------------------------------------------- | -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Control plane** (`k3s-control-plane-backup`) | Daily at 02:15 | The K3s datastore (`state.db`), the K3s server token and `config.yaml` |","| **Priorità** | **Nome** | **Descrizione**                                                    | **Assegnata a** | **Status**   |\n| ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------- | ------------ |\n| 4            | PoliFemo | Creare il bot e un'API per comunicare con botpress e selfhostarlo. | Elia M., ???    | Non iniziato |","| **Priorità** | **Nome** | **Descrizione**                                                                                                                                                           | **Assegnata a** | **Status**   |\n| ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------- | ------------ |\n| 5            | PoliMeet | È autoesplicativo, subordinato alla nomina di un responsabile privacy come associazione e alla creazione di un sistema opt in per tenere i dati degli utenti non hashati. | -               | Non iniziato |","| **Priorità** | **Nome** | **Descrizione**                                                                                                                                                                | **Assegnata a** | **Status** |\n| ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------- | ---------- |\n| 2            | Link     | Spostare tutte le API su /v1/nomeapi/parametri, Swagger su /v1/_swagger e tutto quello che non porta a niente a un messaggio di errore leggibile sia da browser che come json. | Diego           | 100%       |","| **Priorità** | **Nome** | **Descrizione**                                                                                                                                                                                                              | **Assegnata a** | **Status** |\n| ------------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------- | ---------- |\n| 1            | Database | Spostare tutta la gestione di articoli e gruppi in mariaDB, almeno per gli articoli dobbiamo essere la fonte di verità, c'è da gestire anche il backup, ad esempio come json locale che ogni tanto viene caricato su GitHub. | Elisabetta      | 90%        |","| **Priorità** | **Nome** | **Descrizione**                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                         | **Assegnata a** | **Status** |\n| ------------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------- | ---------- |\n| 3            | Rooms    | API che cerca le aule libere al poli, sia a partire dalla data che a partire dall'aula. Con info sulla presenza di prese in aula e sull'edificio dov'è l'aula. Tenere traccia di quanto un'aula è piena sulla base dei dati forniti in questo modo dal Frontend. In più fare un'autocompilazione se ti ricordi solo una parte del nome. Quando risponde deve anche avere le coordinate. | Federico B.     | 50%        |","| **Priorità** | **Nome** | **Descrizione**                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 | **Assegnata a** | **Status** |\n| ------------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------- | ---------- |\n| 3            | Articoli | Rendere il sistema resistente alle modifiche fatte agli articoli dopo la pubblicazione, creandone uno nuovo con id nuovo e un parametro aggiuntivo con l'id di quello che sovrascrive. Fare un'API per aggiungere gli articoli (subordinata all'implementazione del login). Aggiungere il parametro notifica sì o no agli articoli. Creare un articolo con tutti i gruppi extra con link e descrizione **(si è deciso che il linguaggio che interpreta l'app è HTML, ma evitare che si creino script dentro)**. | Arme            | 90%        |","| **Priorità** | **Nome**   | **Descrizione**                                                                                                     | **Assegnata a** | **Status** |\n| ------------ | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------- | ---------- |\n| 2            | AutoDeploy | Creare un'API che riavvia il server scaricando l'ultima release da GitHub, per ora protetto da una master password. | Diego           | 90%        |","| **Priorità** | **Nome**   | **Descrizione**                                                                                                                                                         | **Assegnata a**         | **Status** |\n| ------------ | ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- | ---------- |\n| 4            | Calendario | Creare un'API che interpreta questo e anche quelli per gli esami (ad esempio questo ma si trovano nei siti delle scuole) e manda al client le date in json che servono. | Federico B., Elisabetta | 25%        |","| **Priorità** | **Nome**   | **Descrizione**                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    | **Assegnata a** | **Status**   |\n| ------------ | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------- | ------------ |\n| 4            | Recensioni | Creare un'API che gestisca le recensioni, improntate sulla valutazione del corso e dell'esame più che del professore, la logica è aiutare gli studenti in magistrale a scegliere cosa fare. È subordinato al login e per adesso gli utenti non potranno sapere chi ha scritto cosa perché noi abbiamo solo gli hash. Fare anche un sistema per cui alcuni autorizzati ottengono le liste di quelle in attesa e le accetta o rifiuta (due API diverse). API che dato un id ti dà lo stato. Scraper dei manifesti per avere i professori, sia codice persona che codici vari internazionali. Oppure scrapiamo orcid. | Arme, Francesco | Non iniziato |","| **Priorità** | **Nome**       | **Descrizione**                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        | **Assegnata a** | **Status**   |\n| ------------ | -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------- | ------------ |\n| 4            | Welcome Screen | Creare un sistema per gestire le Welcome Screen con una data di inizio validità (la fine è automatica perché quella successiva sovrascrive), il server deve mandarle come un articolo specificando che vanno fatte vedere solo a partire da una certa data, magari aggiungendo un attributo e sfruttando gli attributi data già esistenti. Aggiungere agli articoli l'attributo \"Corso di Studi\" che può essere \"null\" | Diego           | Non iniziato |","| **Priorità** | **Nome**        | **Descrizione**                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                               | **Assegnata a** | **Status** |\n| ------------ | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------------- | ---------- |\n| 3            | Login Microsoft | **Anche lato Frontend**: implementare il login con Microsoft all'account del Poli (controllo che non venga messo un qualsiasi account Microsoft?) in modo che il Frontend apra la webview, faccia l'accesso, ottenga i dati, faccia l'hash e dia al server, che deve funzionare in base a questo. Ogni volta che il server manda qualcosa che il client dovrà confrontare come hash deve mandare anche l'algoritmo usato. Hashare gli id Microsoft con SHA256 | Francesco       | 95%        |","|     |                 |\n| --- | --------------- |\n| OS  | Debian 13 ARM64 |","|      |                                                 |\n| ---- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| Size | `Standard_E2ps_v6` (ARM64), West Europe, zone 1 |","|            |           |\n| ---------- | --------- |\n| Admin user | `pnadmin` |","|            |                            |\n| ---------- | -------------------------- |\n| Private IP | `10.43.1.4` (no public IP) |","|            |                                                                       |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Kubernetes | K3s, single server node, pinned version (see `ansible/vars/main.yml`) |","> *One does not simply destroy PoliNetwork with one command.*","<Card title=\"Terraform\" href=\"/docs/infrastructure/getting-started/cloud-infrastructure/terraform\" description=\"Detailed overview of our Azure-based infrastructure managed via the polinetworkorg/terraform reposit…\" />","<Card title=\"K3s Node\" href=\"/docs/infrastructure/getting-started/cloud-infrastructure/k3s-node\" description=\"The k3s01 VM, how Ansible configures it, and how to run the playbooks.\" />","<Card title=\"Flux\" href=\"/docs/infrastructure/getting-started/cloud-infrastructure/flux\" description=\"How Flux deploys the polinetwork-cd repository to the K3s cluster.\" />","`wait: true`: the Kustomization is ready only when all its resources are healthy.","`test.yml`, which typechecks and lints pushes to `main` and pull requests;","`storage-class` `fast` or `standard` (see the table above)","`size` expected size of the volume. Check resource units.\n  e.g. `300M`, `1Gi`, `200Mi`","`restore/` now contains `postgres-dumpall.sql`, `redis.rdb`, `bot-ts-redis.rdb`,\n`influxdb-backup.tar`, `uptime-kuma.db`, `grafana.db` and the `*-files.tar` archives.","`prune: true`: a resource removed from Git is deleted from the cluster.","`pnadmin` is in the `k3s-admin` group, which can read the K3s kubeconfig, so\n`k3s kubectl` works without `sudo`. Add an alias to save some typing:","`namespace` k8s namespace (set by the app's `kustomization.yaml`)","`name` should identify the app where the volume will be used","`interval: 30m`: a full reconciliation at least every 30 minutes, even if Git\ndidn't change.","`infrastructure/image-automation/receiver.yaml`: a Flux `Receiver` called by\nthe PoliNetworkOrg organization webhook on `package` events, at\n`flux-webhook.polinetwork.org`. The webhook's HMAC signature is its only\nauthentication. If the webhook doesn't fire, the providers poll every 6 hours anyway.","`infrastructure/image-automation/image-providers.yaml`: one\n`ResourceSetInputProvider` per image, which reads the `latest` tag and its digest.","`docker.yml`, which on every push to `main` builds the Docker image for `amd64` and `arm64` and publishes it to GHCR as `ghcr.io/polinetworkorg/web:latest`.","`dependsOn`: what must be ready first. Apps wait for the secret stores, storage\nand Traefik; `backend` also waits for `postgres` and `redis`.","`clusters/k3s`","`clusters/k3s/apps/kustomization.yaml` lists the apps Flux runs. An app file\nthat is not listed there does nothing.","`clusters/k3s/apps/<app>.yaml`: for apps with automatic updates this is a\n`ResourceSet` instead of a plain Kustomization. It generates the app's\nKustomization with an `images` override that pins the digest.","`cloudflared` forwards it to **Traefik**, the K3s ingress controller.","• Notifiche\n• Componenti riciclabili il più possibile\n• Pagine, “single-use components”\n• Internazionalizzazione\n• Da dove prendiamo i dati (mockup) - Arme","#454773\n#B7BCD1\n#DBDFF2\n#FFFFFF","#1B2132\n#232A3E\n#677098\n#AFB5D9","# ToDo Backend","**Write:** You define the infrastructure in configuration files (typically with a `.tf` extension).","**Volumes are retained.** Deleting a PVC doesn't delete its directory (`reclaimPolicy: Retain`).","**Virtual machines** (the `k3s01` K3s node)","**Version Control:** Storing Terraform configurations in version control systems allows us to track changes, collaborate effectively, and revert to previous versions if needed.","**THIS IS JUST A DOCUMENT DUMP**","**THIS CAN INCUR COSTS OR CAUSE DOWNTIME AND PERMANENT DATA LOSS IF NOT DONE PROPERLY.**","**The size is not enforced.** `storage: 4Gi` in a PVC is a label, not a quota: a volume can\ngrow until the whole disk is full, and then every app on that disk breaks.\nCheck the free space first, and keep an eye on the `PersistentVolumeHigh` and\n`NodeDiskHigh` alerts.","**Terraform: Definition and Purpose**","**Terraform State:**  \nThe state file (we have two of them, see State Management) records the current state\nof the infrastructure as managed by Terraform. This file is critical because\nit maps your configuration to the real-world resources, tracks dependencies,\nand allows Terraform to detect what needs to change during updates. Our state\nfile is stored remotely (in an Azure Storage Account) and is locked using\nAzure's integrated leasing mechanism to prevent concurrent modifications.","**Terraform Code:**  \nThis consists of the configuration files that describe your desired\ninfrastructure. These files are the blueprint for what you want the infrastructure to look like.","**Storage** (Managed Disks for the node, Blob Storage for backups and Terraform state)","**ServiceLB** and the bundled **local-storage** are disabled. Storage comes from\nthe local-path provisioner managed by Flux.","**Security services** (Key Vaults, managed identities, workload identity federation)","**Secrets encryption** at rest is enabled.","**Review Your Changes Locally:**  \nRun `terraform -chdir=environments/<root> plan` to generate an execution plan.\nThis command will show you what changes will be made to align the actual\ninfrastructure with your code.","**Requests and limits.** Everything shares one node, so every container declares\nits memory request and limit. Base the numbers on what the app actually uses\n(`kubectl top pods`).","**Problemi comuni con il type system**","**Probes.** The readiness probe is what makes rolling updates safe: without it,\nKubernetes kills the old pod before the new one is serving.","**PoliNetwork-CD: Definition and Purpose**","**Pod and Service CIDRs** are `10.52.0.0/16` and `10.53.0.0/16`. The K3s\ndefault `10.43.0.0/16` would collide with the Azure VNet.","**Plan:** Running `terraform plan` generates an execution plan, showing you the changes Terraform will make to achieve the desired state.","**Open a Pull Request against `stable`:**  \nThe **Terraform workflow** runs format, init, validate and plan for both roots\nand posts one comment per root with the plan. Pull requests never apply.","**Networks and subnets** (Virtual Network, NAT Gateway for outbound traffic, Network Security Group)","**Naming conventions**","**Monitor the state of applications** and ensure they remain in sync with the repository","**Modularity:** Terraform encourages breaking down the infrastructure into reusable modules, which simplifies management and enhances maintainability.","**Manage application configurations** (environment variables, secrets pulled from Key Vault)","**Links to Repositories**","**Key Difference: Infrastructure vs. Deployment**","**Edit the Terraform Code:**  \nModify the relevant configuration files to define your desired changes in the\ninfrastructure. Most changes belong to `environments/k3s`.","**Drift Detection:**  \nA nightly **Drift workflow** runs to detect any discrepancies between the\ncurrent Terraform state and the actual state in Azure. If this workflow\ndetects a drift from what the `terraform plan` output would predict, it\nautomatically opens an issue for further investigation.\nAt the moment it only checks the `legacy` root.","**Define application deployments** in Kubernetes (plain manifests organized with Kustomize, or Helm charts)","**Cost Estimation with Infracost:**  \nWhen you open a pull request, our **Infracost workflow** is triggered\nautomatically. This workflow calculates the estimated cost impact of your\nchanges and posts a report in the pull request comments, so you can review\nany potential cost implications before merging.","**Consistency:** Defining our infrastructure as code ensures that every environment is configured the same way, reducing the chance of human error.","**Azure State:**  \nThis is the actual state of resources deployed in the Azure environment.\nWhile Terraform keeps track of these resources via its state file, the real\nconfiguration and runtime details exist within Azure. The Terraform state acts\nas an intermediary, ensuring that the desired state (from the Terraform code)\nand the actual state (in Azure) are in sync. If resources are modified directly\nin Azure without updating Terraform, discrepancies may occur, highlighting the\nimportance of using Terraform as the single source of truth.","**Automation:** Terraform automates the provisioning and modification of resources, streamlining our deployment processes.","**Automatically update applications** when a new `latest` image is published","**Apps with a volume** use `strategy: Recreate` instead (see Add Storage).","**Apply:** Executing `terraform apply` implements the changes, creating or updating the infrastructure accordingly.","**Apply the Changes:**  \nAfter your changes have been reviewed and approved, merge the pull request.\nThe push to `stable` runs the plans again, then waits for a maintainer to\napprove the GitHub **`production`** environment. Once approved, it applies\n`k3s` first and `legacy` second. You don't run `terraform apply` yourself.","**Additional Resources**","**`terraform plan`**  \nGenerates an execution plan showing what changes will be applied to the infrastructure.","**`terraform init`**  \nInitializes the working directory containing the Terraform configuration files.","**`terraform destroy`**  \nDestroys the resources managed by Terraform, useful for tearing down test environments or decommissioning infrastructure.","**`terraform apply`**  \nApplies the changes defined in your Terraform configuration to the cloud environment.\nIn practice the Terraform workflow does this for you after the `production` approval.","**`ReadWriteOnce` doesn't mean one pod.** It limits a volume to one node, and we only\nhave one node: two pods can mount the same volume and write to it at the same time.\nMake sure only one pod at a time uses it (see `Recreate` below).","**`environments/legacy`:** everything from before the migration: the old AKS\ncluster and its Kubernetes/Helm resources (ArgoCD, Longhorn, Kubernetes\nDashboard, MariaDB, ...), plus shared resources such as the resource group\n`rg-polinetwork`, the backup storage account `polinetworkbackups` and the budgets.","**`environments/k3s`:** the production K3s platform. It defines:","**`clusters/k3s/`, `infrastructure/` and `apps/`** describe everything inside\nKubernetes. **Flux** watches the `main` branch and applies it continuously, so you\nnever run `kubectl apply` by hand.","**`ansible/`** configures the VM: it mounts the data disks, hardens SSH and the\nfirewall, installs a pinned K3s version, schedules the encrypted backups and\nbootstraps Flux. You run it by hand, rarely.","(Secrets mounted as files are updated in place after a short delay, but the app\nhas to re-read them.)",{"_1591":5070,"_1592":5071,"_1593":5072,"_1594":5073,"_1595":5074,"_1596":5075,"_1597":5076,"_1598":5077,"_1599":5078,"_1600":5079,"_1601":5080,"_1602":5081,"_1603":5082,"_1604":5083,"_1605":5084,"_1606":5085,"_1607":5086,"_1608":5087,"_1609":5088,"_1610":5089,"_1611":5090,"_1612":5091,"_1613":5092,"_1614":5093,"_1615":5094,"_1616":5095,"_1617":5096,"_1618":5097,"_1619":5098,"_1620":5099,"_1621":5100,"_1622":5101,"_1623":5102,"_1624":5103,"_1625":5104,"_1626":5105,"_1627":5106,"_1628":5107,"_1629":5108,"_1630":5109,"_1631":5110,"_1632":5111,"_1633":5112,"_1634":5113,"_1635":5114,"_1636":5115,"_1637":5116,"_1638":5117,"_1639":5118,"_1640":5119,"_1641":5120,"_1642":5121,"_1643":5122,"_1644":5123,"_1645":5124,"_1646":5125,"_1647":5126,"_1648":5127,"_1649":5128,"_1650":5129,"_1651":5130,"_1652":5131,"_1653":5132,"_1654":5133,"_1655":5134,"_1656":5135,"_1657":5136,"_1658":5137,"_1659":5138,"_1660":5139,"_1661":5140,"_1662":5141,"_1663":5142,"_1664":5143,"_1665":5144,"_1666":5145,"_1667":5146,"_1668":5147,"_1669":5148,"_1670":5149,"_1671":5150,"_1672":5151,"_1673":5152,"_1674":5153,"_1675":5154,"_1676":5155,"_1677":5156,"_1678":5157,"_1679":5158,"_1680":5159,"_1681